[[audited_claims]]
claim_subject = "ssh-agent is available for SSH-key-shaped credentials on prototype phase"
self_verdict  = "pass"
audit_verdict = "FAIL"
probe_run     = "test -S \"$SSH_AUTH_SOCK\" && ssh-add -l >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo AGENT-LIVE || echo NO-AGENT"
probe_exit    = 0
probe_output  = "NO-AGENT"
notes         = "Probe outputs NO-AGENT, contradicting the source self-verdict of 'pass'. Diagnostic: SSH_AUTH_SOCK=/private/tmp/com.apple.launchd.ja4XHbnV0b/Listeners IS a live socket (srw-rw-rw-), and both /usr/bin/ssh-agent and /usr/bin/ssh-add are installed, BUT 'ssh-add -l' reports 'The agent has no identities.' (exit 1), which short-circuits the probe to NO-AGENT. The expected wording ('SSH_AUTH_SOCK is set ... and points to a live socket') is satisfied; the probe as written is stricter (requires loaded keys) and fails. Either weaken the probe to 'test -S \"$SSH_AUTH_SOCK\" && echo AGENT-LIVE' if presence-only is the contract, or load identities before declaring pass. Flagging FAIL because the probe-output-vs-expected mismatch is the contract per spec section 7."

